1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,970
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:03,680
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:08,610
(Episode 39)

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,780
He jotted down that address.

6
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:14,120
I'm guessing that's where he went.

7
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,900
Excuse me, can I ask you something?

8
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:33,940
Sure, how can I help you?

9
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,340
Was there a patient here...

10
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:39,580
named Joo Ae Sook?

11
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:41,980
Joo Ae Sook?

12
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:43,820
Yes.

13
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,280
From about 30 years ago.

14
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:48,950
Dad.

15
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:19,580
Why are you here, Dad?

16
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:24,020
I thought I told you
where you should wait.

17
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,390
Oh, right.

18
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:32,400
I've been looking for you
everywhere.

19
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:34,430
Let's go.

20
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:36,530
Have a good day.

21
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,480
I thought I was clear.

22
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,450
I'm the type of person...

23
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,490
who really respects his elders.

24
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:55,550
Please...

25
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:57,490
Mr. Choi...

26
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,360
Clench your jaw.

27
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:36,900
I told you to stay put.

28
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,960
Why do you keep acting up?

29
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:40,700
No, Mr. Choi, it's not that.

30
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:45,140
I only went there hoping to find
some trace of my daughter.

31
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:49,070
Oh, is that so?

32
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:54,250
You beat up your pregnant wife,

33
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,250
and now you're curious
about your kid?

34
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,790
Back then, I was young
and hot-headed,

35
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:02,350
and I wasn't thinking straight.

36
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:05,160
But I'm still the father.

37
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:08,130
I should know
if she's dead or alive.

38
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,100
Even if your daughter's alive,

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,670
would she really welcome
a parent like you?

40
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:22,540
A parent like you is better off
not existing.

41
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,010
Mr. Choi...

42
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,550
Of course. I was wrong.

43
00:03:28,950 --> 00:03:33,590
Don't try anything stupid,
and just stay put quietly.

44
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,090
If you run off anywhere...

45
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:37,890
You know, right?

46
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:41,290
These days,
locating someone like you...

47
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,030
is no trouble at all.

48
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:44,700
Right. I understand.

49
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,530
I won't go anywhere.

50
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:50,340
Actually, I know I should stay put.

51
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,870
You heard what Ms. Joo said, right?

52
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,140
She'd kindly pour concrete
and bury you herself.

53
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:59,040
If you keep acting up like this,

54
00:04:00,810 --> 00:04:02,610
I'm heading out to buy cement.

55
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,750
Wait.

56
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:09,690
I'm never moving another step
from this place.

57
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:13,220
Did you take your medicine?

58
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:16,190
I did,

59
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,230
but I'm still a little dizzy.

60
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:23,330
Then don't sit around like this
and see a doctor.

61
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,440
A doctor can't help.

62
00:04:27,170 --> 00:04:28,640
This has to be my punishment.

63
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:33,180
I hurt you,
so now I'm paying the price.

64
00:04:34,910 --> 00:04:35,980
So,

65
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:39,380
I can't get better
unless you accept my apology.

66
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:43,190
Since you took medicine,
your fever will go down soon.

67
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:44,760
Director Joo will be back soon, too.

68
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:46,390
Get some rest.

69
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:47,790
Seok Jin.

70
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,330
We're not ending things
like this, right?

71
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,560
We've been together
for a really long time.

72
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,500
It's not like we were
just dating for a bit,

73
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:57,470
we even promised to get married.

74
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:02,470
Any relationship can end
in an instant.

75
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:06,680
I'll do anything for you.

76
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,810
I promise.

77
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,020
I'll never speak poorly
of Ms. Park again.

78
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,590
I love you
with all my heart, Seok Jin.

79
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:16,420
You know how I feel, right?

80
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:19,190
Get some rest.

81
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,130
I'm the official heir of Cheongma.

82
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,860
Marrying me means...

83
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,900
you become the true owner
of Cheongma.

84
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,130
Don't you want it too, Seok Jin?

85
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,260
Just stop thinking for today
and get some rest.

86
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,660
Thanks, Seok Jin.

87
00:05:57,630 --> 00:05:58,630
I'll get going.

88
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:07,440
So he actually came over?

89
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:11,110
Yes, pretending to be sick
seemed to work.

90
00:06:11,210 --> 00:06:12,940
He didn't push me away like before.

91
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,380
Right, I'm sure he didn't.

92
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:18,320
What I said must have worked,

93
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:22,120
as it was a tempting offer
Chief Cha couldn't pass up.

94
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,060
I feel like Seok Jin and I can
get back to how we used to be.

95
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:30,390
No, don't drop your guard just yet.

96
00:06:31,230 --> 00:06:34,270
You need to give Chief Cha
a stronger bait.

97
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,930
As in what?

98
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:40,840
Make a clear appeal to the CEO.
Tell him you want Chief Cha.

99
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:42,970
With the CEO's backing,

100
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:45,110
you need to completely win
Chief Cha over.

101
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,650
If the bait comes from the CEO,

102
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:50,150
Chief Cha won't suspect a thing
and will easily bite.

103
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:52,350
You think so?

104
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:57,320
Actually, Dad's been pushing
Seok Jin away recently,

105
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,720
and Seok Jin seemed
really bothered by it.

106
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:03,160
Right, so use that relationship
to your advantage.

107
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:07,060
If you do, you won't need to try
as hard as you're doing now.

108
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,970
You're the best, Ms. Joo.

109
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:12,000
I'm so glad to have you by my side.

110
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:17,340
Don't you go anywhere
and stay right by my side. Okay?

111
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:19,610
Where would I go at this point?

112
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:22,710
After everything I did to get here?

113
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:25,480
Don't worry.

114
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,450
I'm not going anywhere.

115
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,450
Thank you, Ms. Joo.

116
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,460
What, an OB-GYN?

117
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:36,960
Yes, it seems
he visited a hospital...

118
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:38,760
near where you used to live.

119
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,430
There was only one hospital there
30 years ago,

120
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:46,240
so he must assume
you gave birth there.

121
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,610
Then,

122
00:07:51,210 --> 00:07:52,580
did the baby really...

123
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,510
I was beaten every single day.

124
00:07:56,810 --> 00:07:58,380
How could the baby have been fine?

125
00:08:00,590 --> 00:08:01,620
All right.

126
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:04,890
Keep an even closer eye
on An Guk Cheol.

127
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:07,160
Sure, I'll do that.

128
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:16,100
What does he even want
with my daughter?

129
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,710
After all this time,
that monster wants to play father?

130
00:08:21,810 --> 00:08:23,110
Don't make me laugh.

131
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,180
If you ever come near my daughter,

132
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:29,410
I'll take your life that very day.

133
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:32,520
Given the tendencies
of the three directors,

134
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,550
they prioritize numbers
over justification.

135
00:08:34,850 --> 00:08:36,990
We should persuade them
with the return on investment.

136
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:39,790
I suppose so.

137
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:42,660
I'm asking this just in case.

138
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,700
While getting ready
for the board meeting,

139
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:48,170
you didn't reach out to any
of the other directors, right?

140
00:08:48,370 --> 00:08:49,900
No, not at all.

141
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:52,570
But why do you ask?

142
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:56,340
The Chairman specifically
emphasized it one more time.

143
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:59,540
That's why I'm being
extra careful these days.

144
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:03,780
I even have the other secretaries
deliver other announcements for me.

145
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:05,850
I see.

146
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:11,660
Why do you like Chief Cha so much?

147
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:14,490
Why reject
all the other eligible bachelors...

148
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:17,500
and insist on marrying only him?

149
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:19,530
I have my reasons.

150
00:09:19,930 --> 00:09:23,230
Seok Jin is the most
cost-effective option I have.

151
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,940
Why would you even consider that?

152
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,100
You have all the power.

153
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:28,740
Just think about it.

154
00:09:29,010 --> 00:09:31,380
Those men from good families
you keep talking about?

155
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,740
Imagine how much I'd suffer
marrying into a family like that.

156
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:35,910
That's not the case with Seok Jin.

157
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:39,880
Even without trying hard,
I'll always be above him.

158
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,120
So,

159
00:09:42,190 --> 00:09:45,260
since Chief Cha will always
be beneath you,

160
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:48,130
you want to marry him?

161
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,190
Yes.

162
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:50,930
And above all,

163
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:53,430
I don't want to live
fighting like you and Mom.

164
00:09:53,430 --> 00:09:56,400
Come on, we don't fight that much.

165
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:58,200
Like I don't know.

166
00:09:58,570 --> 00:10:02,740
You two have been subtly fighting
over the company since I was young.

167
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:05,180
I suffered a lot
from all that tension.

168
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,850
At least if I marry Seok Jin,

169
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:09,450
there won't be any power struggles.

170
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:11,280
Well, this is a surprise.

171
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,520
I didn't know my daughter
put so much thought into things.

172
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:15,850
There's that, but also...

173
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:18,020
I just want him.

174
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:21,760
Ever since I was young,
you let me have everything I wanted.

175
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:22,830
No matter what it was.

176
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:29,100
As for Cha Seok Jin,
let's wait and see for now.

177
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:35,040
Why don't we have dinner
with Seok Jin's mom this weekend?

178
00:10:35,410 --> 00:10:37,840
We've never invited her
to our house before.

179
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,710
Specific triggers can cause
those sealed memories...

180
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,420
to come back at any moment.

181
00:10:44,650 --> 00:10:46,750
That said, every case is unique,

182
00:10:46,950 --> 00:10:48,690
so we can't say for sure
when that might happen.

183
00:10:51,890 --> 00:10:55,230
If she's a ticking time bomb
waiting to explode,

184
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:59,160
keeping her close and watching her
might not be a bad idea.

185
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:09,140
(Taeseon Hospital)

186
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,420
It's a bit of a hassle,

187
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:24,860
but it doesn't hurt to be sure.

188
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:32,230
Hello.

189
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,100
I'd like to ask you something.

190
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,930
Sure. How can I help you?

191
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,670
I'm looking for someone, you see.

192
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:43,140
A mother who gave birth here
in the past.

193
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:44,480
Excuse me?

194
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:46,440
A friend of mine...

195
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:49,410
gave birth here a long time ago
and then disappeared.

196
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:52,320
- I see.
- I really want to find her.

197
00:11:52,950 --> 00:11:55,620
Is there any way
I could look at the records?

198
00:11:56,090 --> 00:12:00,190
I'm sorry, but we can't disclose
personal information.

199
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:03,330
I figured.

200
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,170
My poor friend, Ae Sook.

201
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:12,600
Do you mean Joo Ae Sook?

202
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:16,040
Actually, a man came by earlier
and asked about her.

203
00:12:16,770 --> 00:12:19,140
Before he could ask anything else,
someone like his son came...

204
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:20,540
and took him away.

205
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,280
Is that so?

206
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:27,150
I guess there's nothing I can do.

207
00:12:28,550 --> 00:12:29,790
One more thing.

208
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:33,890
Before that, a lawyer dropped by.

209
00:12:40,830 --> 00:12:41,970
His name was...

210
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,570
Right. I think it was Seo Hyun Jae.

211
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:48,010
He was also looking for someone
named Joo Ae Sook.

212
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,980
Really?

213
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:55,550
Yes, he made
such an earnest request,

214
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:57,480
but I told him I wasn't allowed
to disclose personal information.

215
00:12:57,850 --> 00:13:00,380
Instead, I gave him
the number of the nurse...

216
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:02,720
who was working here at the time.

217
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:06,290
The nurse's number?

218
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:11,560
Why is Team Leader Seo
digging into my past?

219
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:15,030
Even if he's helping Ko Eun Seol,

220
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:18,200
there's no reason for him
to dig into my past.

221
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:21,940
Could it be...

222
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:26,140
Did he find out something
while looking into Manager Na?

223
00:13:29,450 --> 00:13:30,850
Ko Eun Seol, Seo Hyun Jae.

224
00:13:31,450 --> 00:13:33,780
How dare the two of them
try to screw me over?

225
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:35,550
Darn it!

226
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:37,020
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

227
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:39,020
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

228
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:49,270
It's me. Get to my office right now.

229
00:14:41,090 --> 00:14:42,990
Why isn't she back yet?

230
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:46,790
It's way past dinnertime,
and she's especially late today.

231
00:14:48,290 --> 00:14:51,660
Mom, I'm hungry.
Let's go inside and eat.

232
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,130
We'll cook ourselves some ramyeon.

233
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,800
Just hold on.

234
00:14:56,170 --> 00:14:59,800
If we just hang tight here
until the landlady gets back,

235
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:04,840
we can casually join her for dinner.

236
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:07,440
Mom, are we beggars or something?

237
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,150
What do you mean, beggars?

238
00:15:09,210 --> 00:15:11,020
I wouldn't do this without a plan.

239
00:15:11,650 --> 00:15:13,220
Not that you'd know.

240
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:16,120
What plan?
A plan to leech a free dinner?

241
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,890
Instead of saying we want to eat,

242
00:15:18,990 --> 00:15:21,560
we'll say Eun Guk wants us
to eat together.

243
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:24,500
She'll walk right in
and invite us to join.

244
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:27,800
Wait, if Eun Guk says
he wants to eat,

245
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:30,870
Teun Teun's Mom will set
the table for him right away?

246
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,940
Of course. Just wait and see.

247
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:37,410
Why? Why would she
set the table for Eun Guk?

248
00:15:37,710 --> 00:15:40,310
Gosh, how slow are you?

249
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,250
Being so clueless
is why you can't land a job.

250
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:47,580
Is it because they're coworkers?

251
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:50,920
Still, I don't think
she'll cook for him.

252
00:15:51,190 --> 00:15:53,720
Want to bet? 50 dollars.

253
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,660
Sure, let's bet.

254
00:15:57,590 --> 00:15:59,230
Hello, ma'am.

255
00:15:59,230 --> 00:16:01,200
Hey, Teun Teun. It's been a while.

256
00:16:01,570 --> 00:16:03,300
What were you two doing out here?

257
00:16:03,970 --> 00:16:06,600
Are you just getting home?
Did you eat?

258
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,270
I'm about to eat now.

259
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:10,970
Ms. Seo, what are you going
to do for dinner?

260
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,910
We're going to go in and eat now.

261
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:15,380
Gosh, that works out perfectly.

262
00:16:15,450 --> 00:16:18,850
We haven't eaten yet either,
so we can all eat together.

263
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:20,520
What?

264
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:22,990
Did you leave your rice with me
or something?

265
00:16:23,050 --> 00:16:24,250
Eat together, my foot.

266
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,860
Exactly. Why are you
bothering my boss?

267
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:28,930
Don't we have any food at home?

268
00:16:29,930 --> 00:16:31,630
Actually, we don't.

269
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,060
If it's too much trouble,

270
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,530
we can just grab some cup noodles.

271
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,570
Darn, I was really craving
a proper meal.

272
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:41,070
What can we do, right?

273
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:44,410
Then,

274
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:47,510
why don't we just
whip something up to eat?

275
00:16:49,150 --> 00:16:51,420
Sounds good. Let's all eat together.

276
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,750
I suppose we could do that.

277
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:55,420
Boss, you don't have to do this.

278
00:16:55,850 --> 00:16:56,950
We'll just eat by ourselves.

279
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:59,190
It's better than leaving
leftover rice.

280
00:16:59,390 --> 00:17:01,020
Let's go. Come on.

281
00:17:03,830 --> 00:17:05,230
Where do you think you're going?

282
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:06,460
What?

283
00:17:06,630 --> 00:17:07,630
Pay up.

284
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,130
Seriously?

285
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,770
One, two, three, four, five.

286
00:17:21,150 --> 00:17:23,410
Are you trying to cheat
your own mother?

287
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,480
Hand it over. You're one short.

288
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:29,520
Call it a family discount.

289
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,390
Seriously.
You're absolutely ruthless.

290
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:47,140
Is this for my husband?

291
00:17:48,410 --> 00:17:49,410
Yes.

292
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:51,880
He hasn't been able
to sleep at all lately.

293
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,180
Even so,
this liquor is really strong.

294
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,010
He doesn't drink too much.

295
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,020
He said just one glass
helps him sleep soundly.

296
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,900
From now on,
prepare warm tea instead.

297
00:18:14,670 --> 00:18:16,470
Yes, I'll do that.

298
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:20,600
And Director Joo.

299
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:23,870
I'll handle this from now on,

300
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:26,080
so you don't need
to bother with it anymore.

301
00:18:27,950 --> 00:18:29,050
It only makes sense.

302
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:31,480
My husband is having
trouble sleeping.

303
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,490
Naturally, as his wife, I should
be the one taking care of him.

304
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:38,320
I'll make his tea,

305
00:18:39,020 --> 00:18:40,690
so you can go get some rest.

306
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,830
Sure, I'll go to my room then.

307
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,780
Oh, right. Come in, Director Joo.

308
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,150
Director Joo?

309
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:10,750
Has she been coming by
every day at this hour?

310
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:12,020
Right.

311
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:14,960
She's been bringing me
my supplements and stuff.

312
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:16,230
I see.

313
00:19:16,730 --> 00:19:18,060
You should've asked me instead.

314
00:19:20,330 --> 00:19:21,730
It's warm tea.

315
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:26,240
It's far less harsh on your system
than strong liquor.

316
00:19:27,870 --> 00:19:29,040
Right, thanks.

317
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:34,480
Have you been relying on alcohol
to help you fall asleep?

318
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:38,920
It's just that
I've had a lot of work lately.

319
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:43,050
Do you realize how dangerous
having a drink before bed can be?

320
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:47,660
You'll get addicted to it
without even realizing it.

321
00:19:49,190 --> 00:19:50,430
No more drinking.

322
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:55,570
From now on,
I'll make you warm tea every day.

323
00:19:56,830 --> 00:19:58,870
Sure. Thanks for that.

324
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:01,510
And you should obviously
ask me to do this.

325
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:06,110
Don't bother Director Joo
by calling her in so late.

326
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,750
That's an abuse of power.

327
00:20:11,450 --> 00:20:13,520
First on today's agenda
is the approval...

328
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:16,420
of the scholarship program tied
to correctional rehabilitation.

329
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:21,060
This proposal is a new project
to boost the social public value...

330
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:23,090
of the Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation...

331
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:26,600
while helping prevent recidivism
and aiding social reintegration.

332
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:30,870
Then we'll proceed with voting
on this agenda item.

333
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,570
(Against)

334
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:45,020
(For)

335
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,950
The vote stands at three in favor...

336
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:52,720
and four opposed
out of seven members present.

337
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:55,530
Consequently, the first agenda item,

338
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,000
approval of the scholarship program...

339
00:20:58,060 --> 00:20:59,500
linked to correctional rehabilitation,

340
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:02,330
has been rejected.

341
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,320
Don't be too discouraged.

342
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:23,050
We can make up for what we lacked...

343
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:26,020
and pass it
at the next board meeting.

344
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:30,860
According to the rules,
we still have one more chance.

345
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:35,130
Yes, this gave me a chance to see
what we were lacking.

346
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,670
By the next meeting,

347
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:39,200
I plan to attach
the project monitoring data as well.

348
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:42,140
Yes, that sounds good.

349
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:45,010
Let's turn this crisis
into an opportunity...

350
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:47,140
and work even harder.

351
00:21:47,810 --> 00:21:51,880
Yes, I'll run around
and help you both.

352
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:56,850
Thank you, Secretary Choi.
I feel reassured thanks to you.

353
00:21:58,820 --> 00:21:59,820
Not at all.

354
00:22:03,130 --> 00:22:06,230
How could you vote in favor
after taking that from CEO Kang?

355
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:08,770
All the directors got it.

356
00:22:09,130 --> 00:22:10,830
Right. We all did.

357
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:13,340
Even if the Chairman
has Cheongma blood,

358
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,940
look at how the company
is being run.

359
00:22:15,770 --> 00:22:17,140
Everyone is aligned with the CEO.

360
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:19,340
Is Director Joo also
one of the CEO's people?

361
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:22,410
I heard her secretary handed out
all the gifts.

362
00:22:23,210 --> 00:22:24,210
Is that so?

363
00:22:30,590 --> 00:22:32,190
Is Director Joo also
one of the CEO's people?

364
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:34,660
I heard her secretary handed out
all the gifts.

365
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:37,190
Ko Eun Seol.

366
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,940
I heard the scholarship program
you prepared was rejected today.

367
00:22:51,210 --> 00:22:53,880
We can reintroduce the agenda
at the next board meeting.

368
00:22:54,410 --> 00:22:55,910
Do you think
it will be approved then?

369
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:58,010
If it were going to pass,
it would've happened already.

370
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:01,920
Ms. Kang.

371
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:05,920
The Chairman is your mother.

372
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:09,690
That was the scholarship program
your mother was pushing for.

373
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:12,000
Are you really that happy
it got rejected?

374
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,900
That's not what I meant.

375
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,400
Even if it gets approved,

376
00:23:17,530 --> 00:23:19,940
how much of a help would you be?

377
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,740
Of course I'm upset it was rejected.
It's my mom's project.

378
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:24,740
Exactly.

379
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,380
It's obviously
something to be upset about,

380
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:29,380
but you don't really look like it.

381
00:23:30,010 --> 00:23:31,010
Whatever.

382
00:23:31,250 --> 00:23:32,920
Now that there are
no outside assignments,

383
00:23:33,050 --> 00:23:34,420
you ought to do
your real work properly.

384
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:38,020
Go and finish the draft
for the next season's design.

385
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:40,360
Sure.

386
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:47,730
Good work.

387
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:50,300
Thanks to your quick actions,

388
00:23:50,730 --> 00:23:53,100
we stopped the scholarship program
without any issues.

389
00:23:55,210 --> 00:23:57,810
I can trust you
with the next board meeting, right?

390
00:23:58,010 --> 00:23:59,010
Yes, ma'am.

391
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,140
The opinions of the directors
we have won over...

392
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,650
won't change much.

393
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:03,980
Good.

394
00:24:04,380 --> 00:24:06,680
If we get through
the next board meeting like this,

395
00:24:07,050 --> 00:24:08,820
the Chairman will lose
her momentum too.

396
00:24:11,990 --> 00:24:14,090
How is An Guk Cheol doing?

397
00:24:14,690 --> 00:24:17,590
When I went there last time,
I taught him a proper lesson.

398
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:20,060
He'll never do
anything foolish again.

399
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:23,000
I also gave a strict warning
to the motel owner.

400
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,600
Good, you did well.

401
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:30,010
(Lee Ji Hye)

402
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:55,870
You put your couple ring back on.

403
00:24:56,930 --> 00:24:58,000
Why, should I take it off again?

404
00:24:59,770 --> 00:25:02,510
Shouldn't you look at someone
when they're talking to you?

405
00:25:03,340 --> 00:25:04,340
Look at me.

406
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,910
It's during work hours.
Shouldn't you be working?

407
00:25:08,350 --> 00:25:11,050
Like I said,
you're my vitamin, Seok Jin.

408
00:25:11,250 --> 00:25:13,380
Seeing you gives me
the energy to do my work.

409
00:25:18,490 --> 00:25:21,860
My dad wants to invite Ms. Park
to our house.

410
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:24,790
What?

411
00:25:25,030 --> 00:25:27,260
We've never invited her
to our house before.

412
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:30,330
I think he's going to bring up
our engagement.

413
00:25:32,240 --> 00:25:33,240
Did the CEO say that?

414
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,140
He's thinking about our engagement?

415
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:37,870
Yes, I told my dad...

416
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:40,240
that I don't want to marry
anyone but you.

417
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:44,710
He seemed to give in and approve it.

418
00:25:48,690 --> 00:25:51,690
Then I'll set a date
for the dinner invitation.

419
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:01,130
Welcome...

420
00:26:09,670 --> 00:26:10,670
What should we get?

421
00:26:12,140 --> 00:26:13,580
I want something sweet.

422
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,950
Honey, let's go somewhere else.

423
00:26:16,780 --> 00:26:17,780
Why?

424
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:20,750
I think I left something in the car.
Let's go.

425
00:26:23,490 --> 00:26:24,490
Bye.

426
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:29,460
Boss, are you okay?

427
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,200
- Boss.
- Yes?

428
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:36,300
What's wrong?

429
00:26:37,130 --> 00:26:39,400
Do you know the people
who just left?

430
00:26:40,570 --> 00:26:42,310
No, I don't.

431
00:27:23,550 --> 00:27:24,550
Hello?

432
00:27:25,150 --> 00:27:26,150
Let's meet up.

433
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:29,090
Forget it.

434
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:30,890
Don't ever call me again.

435
00:27:40,900 --> 00:27:43,270
Don't be too disappointed, honey.

436
00:27:43,830 --> 00:27:45,940
Since the initial vote was 4 to 3,

437
00:27:46,570 --> 00:27:49,740
you definitely have a shot
at winning the next board meeting.

438
00:27:50,010 --> 00:27:52,380
Yes, I think so too.

439
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:56,710
We just need one person
to switch to our side.

440
00:27:58,080 --> 00:28:01,420
Naturally, you and Director Joo
must've voted in favor.

441
00:28:02,050 --> 00:28:06,160
Then out of the remaining directors,
we only need to persuade one person.

442
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:09,260
Right. Yes, of course.

443
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:12,060
Since you always make
the right choices,

444
00:28:12,630 --> 00:28:15,270
the directors will follow your lead.

445
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:18,070
I'm not that worried.

446
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:33,180
I thought you'd be heartbroken,
so I called you over.

447
00:28:34,120 --> 00:28:36,350
Since the scholarship program
you were preparing was rejected,

448
00:28:36,350 --> 00:28:37,420
you must be very upset.

449
00:28:38,590 --> 00:28:40,520
It isn't completely over yet.

450
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:42,960
I'll have to prepare well
for the next board meeting.

451
00:28:43,630 --> 00:28:47,230
You're always so resilient,
Eun Seol.

452
00:28:48,870 --> 00:28:52,270
The foundation's board
is surprisingly pretty conservative.

453
00:28:52,970 --> 00:28:55,540
Swaying such stubborn people
won't be easy.

454
00:28:55,970 --> 00:28:59,140
I'm just worried
you might end up getting hurt.

455
00:29:00,710 --> 00:29:02,450
That's why
at the next board meeting,

456
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:05,250
I'm going to try a different method
to convince the directors.

457
00:29:06,780 --> 00:29:08,220
What kind of method?

458
00:29:09,550 --> 00:29:11,550
I'll tell you when the time comes.

459
00:29:12,290 --> 00:29:13,860
It isn't any fun
if I tell you in advance.

460
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:20,060
Now I'm really curious.
I wonder what you've prepared.

461
00:29:25,140 --> 00:29:27,970
Are you on your way back
from seeing Director Joo?

462
00:29:28,770 --> 00:29:29,770
Yes.

463
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:33,040
Do you want to have dinner
together today?

464
00:29:33,810 --> 00:29:34,810
Sounds good.

465
00:29:35,410 --> 00:29:36,510
Then I'll reach out to you later.

466
00:29:37,580 --> 00:29:38,580
Secretary Choi.

467
00:29:41,020 --> 00:29:42,950
I'm not really feeling dinner,

468
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:45,590
so how about
we grab a drink instead?

469
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:48,020
A drink?

470
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:53,130
Yes, sounds good.

471
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:55,670
Okay, I'll see you later then.

472
00:30:05,510 --> 00:30:08,610
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

473
00:30:13,420 --> 00:30:14,450
Hello, ma'am.

474
00:30:14,920 --> 00:30:16,650
I'm attorney Seo Hyun Jae.

475
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:18,760
I'm calling because...

476
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:22,030
I heard you remember a patient
named Joo Ae Sook from 30 years ago.

477
00:30:24,230 --> 00:30:25,300
If you don't mind,

478
00:30:25,530 --> 00:30:27,460
may I come see you in person
to ask a few questions?

479
00:30:29,970 --> 00:30:30,970
Yes.

480
00:30:32,770 --> 00:30:33,770
Right.

481
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:35,240
Thank you.

482
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:39,180
I'll come over to meet you in person
for a chat.

483
00:30:39,780 --> 00:30:40,810
Sure.

484
00:30:48,150 --> 00:30:49,720
If I bring Director Joo's photo
and check,

485
00:30:49,750 --> 00:30:51,120
I'll be able to confirm...

486
00:30:52,220 --> 00:30:54,190
whether Eun Seol's biological mom,
Joo Ae Sook,

487
00:30:55,430 --> 00:30:56,960
is actually Director Joo Mi Ran.

488
00:30:57,990 --> 00:30:59,400
The phone is turned off...

489
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:20,320
Mr. Seo, what brings you here?

490
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:54,620
(A Trap Called Desire)

491
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:57,420
Why are you taking orders from him
regarding the foundation's work?

492
00:31:57,490 --> 00:32:01,190
Do you honestly think I'd give you
the finance team's work as well?

493
00:32:01,390 --> 00:32:03,460
We're going to Hae Ra's house
together tomorrow.

494
00:32:03,730 --> 00:32:05,190
Why would we go there?

495
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:06,830
Were you
with Secretary Choi yesterday?

496
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,230
Are you two close?

497
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:10,200
Being seen together like that
could hurt your reputation.

498
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:13,570
Is Director Joo sending me
some kind of warning?

499
00:32:13,770 --> 00:32:17,040
I think it's best to keep
your distance from Ms. Joo for now.

500
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,340
Secretary Choi, look into it.

501
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:19,940
Figure out
what Seo Hyun Jae's after.

502
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:21,680
What are you doing here?

503
00:32:22,210 --> 00:32:24,180
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
